  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "core",
  "estimatedMinutes": 25,
  "instructions": "Implement the decorator factory `retry(times, delay=0)` in `main/retry.py`. It validates its arguments as soon as `retry(...)` is called, retries the wrapped function up to `times` attempts with `time.sleep(delay)` between failures, and finally raises `RuntimeError` chained to the last exception. Use `functools.wraps` and `import time` as a module so tests can patch `main.retry.time.sleep`.",
